{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791544767,"nonce":"WVSbkq/dRrnDekIWbxtMu+H+NC0=","message":"Milestone committed locally as 2f56878 (Retain AIR transfer layouts without duplicate opcodes).\n\nOptimized AIR now retains canonical SSA plus compact PC/register maps, rather than a second flat opcode body. Flat consumers serialize on demand. Entry-only compiled functions retire prepared interpreter bodies; active frames retain their own Rc for safe source mapping. Loop bodies remain available for OSR. Decoder completion moves its result rather than cloning the whole program. LLVM shares decoded type metadata and detaches only its type table when mutation is necessary.\n\nValidation: AIR tests (203), retier tests (5), SSA active-frame/invalidation lifetime test, and shared type-table mutation isolation test passed. Eighteen interpreter/Cranelift/LLVM output comparisons matched. Ashui pixel checks passed. A controlled before/after retier run with jit-threshold=1 and opt-threshold=1000000 actually took the source=osr transfer in both binaries and produced the same checksum. This does not establish that the separately tracked threshold=10000 Mac forced-retier gate is fixed.\n\nTwo alternating TreeMotion pairs with the application preset reduced mean physical footprint from 167.73 to 158.95 MiB (8.78 MiB). Idle CPU was 0.00056–0.00081%. Settled malloc attribution dropped from about 78.22 to 71.87 MiB, including AIR from 25.83 to 20.91 MiB. Instrumented vmmap footprints were noisy under system compression; the normal alternating pairs are the footprint evidence.\n\nArtifacts: Ashui .ashui/memory-comparison/half-pair-120631, half-behavior-121010, half-retier-121224, heap-114958, heap-120817, half-pixels.log.\n\nRemaining: the requested roughly half-sized overall footprint is not achieved. Cold interpreted helpers still retain many canonical bodies. Single-run interpreter closure timing and upper frame percentiles were slower/noisy; repeat performance comparisons before calling latency unchanged. Testing reuse of the existing flat walker's loop-free preparation policy next.","files":null}]}